# Whole-store Wattbike Hub pull, once a day, independent of Polar. Triggered by wattbike-pull.timer.
# Install to /etc/systemd/system/ (tooling-pull only refreshes units already installed there).
#
# Why it exists (i-20261127-131157): the only other caller of the pull is wattbike.start() in
# services/forward/polar_fetch.py, gated on Polar reporting a ride. So a ride done with the app
# paired but no Polar strap, a pull that failed or was killed, and Wattbike closing the anonymous
# read all waited for "the next Polar ride", which in 2026-10-19..11-27 was 39+ days away. pull() is
# a whole-store idempotent sync (skips files it holds); a quiet day costs 2 anonymous requests. Its
# journal line ("WATTBIKE: N sessions, 0 new files") is the standing answer to "quiet or stalled",
# and a closed route is a failed unit with its cause at err. Deliberately NOT a freshness lane: the
# store cannot grow without a ride, so a lane would fire on every idle week.
[Unit]
Description=moprox Wattbike Hub pull (daily whole-store sync, independent of Polar)
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target
[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=mikael
Environment=HOME=/home/mikael
Environment=PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1
ExecStart=/usr/bin/python3 /opt/moprox-tooling/services/training/wattbike.py
